WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.223
The house looked and smelled very old.

2
00:00:05.224 --> 00:00:10.286
Eleven-year-old Vinnie didn’t want to live there.

3
00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:14.367
Neither did his nine-year-old sister, Mandy.

4
00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:17.473
But the children had no choice.

5
00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:24.162
Six months ago their parents gave them some shocking news.

6
00:00:24.163 --> 00:00:27.802
"We’re moving to the country," they announced.

7
00:00:27.803 --> 00:00:31.900
"Why?" asked the startled children.

8
00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:36.216
"You need the fresh air," Mom explained.

9
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:40.606
"You’re going to love the new house," added Dad.

10
00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:45.269
"But what about our friends?" Vinnie and Mandy cried.

11
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.219
"You’ll make new ones," said Mom firmly.

12
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.238
The family arrived at their "new" house.

13
00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:57.749
It was actually a hundred years old.

14
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.743
It needed many repairs.

15
00:01:00.744 --> 00:01:05.340
Mom and Dad got busy painting the outside of the house.

16
00:01:05.341 --> 00:01:09.169
Vinnie and Mandy had lots to do inside.

17
00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.610
"Vinnie?" Mandy walked into the living room.

18
00:01:13.611 --> 00:01:17.940
Her brother was tearing old wallpaper from the wall.

19
00:01:17.941 --> 00:01:21.873
"What?" he asked, annoyed at everything.

20
00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:25.067
Vinnie threw down the scraper.

21
00:01:25.068 --> 00:01:27.876
"This is a stupid house!"

22
00:01:27.877 --> 00:01:32.875
"Well, complaining isn’t going to help," said Mandy.

23
00:01:32.876 --> 00:01:35.654
Vinnie shrugged.

24
00:01:35.655 --> 00:01:40.875
"Dad said I have to clean out the attic," Mandy continued.

25
00:01:40.876 --> 00:01:45.237
"But I’m scared to go up there by myself."

26
00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:48.079
"You aren’t afraid of ghosts, are you?"

27
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.357
Vinnie grabbed an old sheet from one of the chairs.

28
00:01:52.358 --> 00:01:55.074
He pulled it over his head.

29
00:01:55.075 --> 00:01:59.727
Flinging his arms in the air, he made scary noises.

30
00:01:59.728 --> 00:02:04.237
Grinning, Mandy pulled the sheet off Vinnie’s head.

31
00:02:04.238 --> 00:02:10.880
"Will you come with me or not?" she asked.

32
00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:15.865
Vinnie led the way upstairs.

33
00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:22.418
In the dusty attic, they were surrounded by books, maps, and cobwebs.

34
00:02:22.419 --> 00:02:25.866
Vinnie did not like spiders.

35
00:02:25.867 --> 00:02:31.145
He brushed a sticky spider web off his face.

36
00:02:31.146 --> 00:02:34.734
Mandy was more interested in the books.

37
00:02:34.735 --> 00:02:43.367
They were everywhere—in boxes, on shelves, and in tall piles against the wall.

38
00:02:43.368 --> 00:02:47.935
"Oh!" she said clapping her hands excitedly.

39
00:02:47.936 --> 00:02:50.756
Mandy loved to read.

40
00:02:50.757 --> 00:02:56.141
"Do we know anything about the owner of this house?" she asked.

41
00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.382
Vinnie shook his head.

42
00:02:58.383 --> 00:03:01.025
"Maybe he was a writer."

43
00:03:01.026 --> 00:03:04.336
Then he looked around for creepy spiders.

44
00:03:04.337 --> 00:03:07.990
Mandy read the book titles in one box.

45
00:03:07.991 --> 00:03:11.874
All the books were about history or traveling.

46
00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:18.700
"Well, he must have loved history," she said.

47
00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:22.828
Vinnie walked over to a shelf of books.

48
00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:27.163
"Mandy, look at this!" Vinnie called, excitedly.

49
00:03:27.164 --> 00:03:30.669
He held a thick, dusty green album.

50
00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.538
The children flipped through the first few pages.

51
00:03:34.539 --> 00:03:38.385
Each page had one black-and-white photograph.

52
00:03:38.386 --> 00:03:41.918
Something was written below each photo.

53
00:03:41.919 --> 00:03:44.890
"I wonder if this is the owner."

54
00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:49.426
Mandy pointed to the elderly man in one of the pictures.

55
00:03:49.427 --> 00:03:53.338
He had a friendly smile.

56
00:03:53.339 --> 00:03:56.363
Vinnie turned to the first page.

57
00:03:56.364 --> 00:04:00.554
"Hey, Mandy," said Vinnie, "look at this one.

58
00:04:00.555 --> 00:04:02.420
He’s in a boat and . . ."

59
00:04:02.421 --> 00:04:04.813
Vinnie looked closer.

60
00:04:04.814 --> 00:04:09.218
"Cool! Here’s a pyramid and an eagle in the background.

61
00:04:09.219 --> 00:04:12.338
He must be in Egypt."

62
00:04:12.339 --> 00:04:19.683
"Vinnie, this picture is . . ." Mandy paused. "different."

63
00:04:19.684 --> 00:04:23.334
"What do you mean?" asked Vinnie.

64
00:04:23.335 --> 00:04:27.874
Mandy rubbed her eyes and stared at the photo again.

65
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:38.777
"Look at the pyramid," she whispered. "It’s glowing."

